  "notes": "Modified cash basis village, FY ended Sept 30, 2025. Governmental beginning/ending are the governmental funds fund balances (p4), which include cash, CDs and restricted cash net of payables. Business-type measure is net position (modified cash); no single total receipts printed so receipts/disbursements totals computed. Capital grants and loan payments recorded as receipts/disbursements so roll-forward 655,853+212,804-242,008+9,511=636,160 holds. The governmental total column prints transfers in 218,986 and out 228,497 (net 9,511 to enterprise funds). Budgetary comparison p7 (report p17) is recorded in detail (actual budgetary basis, final budget): governmental functions plus Transfers -100,292 (other financing, inside the printed governmental total 595,803), and Sewer/Water/Trash (business-type total 242,008); Total disbursements 837,811 = 595,803 + 242,008. Its single receipts line, Receipts and transfers 860,035 (budget 652,922), combines all funds' receipts with transfers in and has no breakdown, so it is not in detail (it cannot be put in revenue or other financing without guessing a split; the statement receipts and transfers_in hold the figures). The Statement of Activities (p2, report p5, gained in the v7 re-trim) labels the governmental Taxes line as Property taxes 85,054, so it is categorized as property tax; it adds no other new lines (its figures match pp4 and 6). Read pages 1-7 of 7"
